Call `reverse()` on a mutable vector to reverse it in place:

```rust
let mut v = vec![1, 2, 3];
v.reverse();
assert_eq!(v, [3, 2, 1]);
```

Or iterate backwards with `v.iter().rev()` if you don't want to modify it.

```rust
fn is_prime(n: u64) -> bool {
    if n < 2 {
        return false;
    }
    let mut d = 2;
    while d * d <= n {
        if n % d == 0 {
            return false;
        }
        d += 1;
    }
    true
}
```

